{"id": "EUVD-2026-55512", "enisaUuid": "adf77e3c-f466-3de8-87a3-0b9a581915c1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrbd: Reset positive result codes to zero in object map update path\n\nIn a reply message to an RBD request, a positive result code indicates\na data payload, which is not allowed for writes. While\nrbd_osd_req_callback() already resets a positive result code for writes\nto zero, rbd_object_map_callback() does not. This allows a corrupted\nreply to an object map update to trigger the rbd_assert(*result < 0) in\n__rbd_obj_handle_request(). This happens, because\nrbd_object_map_callback() calls rbd_obj_handle_request() ->\n__rbd_obj_handle_request() and passes this positive result code. From\n__rbd_obj_handle_request(), rbd_obj_advance_write() is called, which\nleaves the positive result code unchanged and returns true. Therefore,\nthe if(done && *result) branch is executed in __rbd_obj_handle_request()\nand the assertion triggers.\n\nThis patch fixes the issue by adjusting the logic in the\nrbd_object_map_callback() path. A positive result code for an object map\nupdate is now reset to zero (similar to rbd_osd_req_callback()), and the\nmessage is subsequently handled the same way as if the result code was\nzero from the beginning. Additionally, a WARN_ON_ONCE() is added for\nthis case.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:58:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:58:52", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf1167292f606deaddac35ec384eba48f08a68d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da926959bf791441ba06a80571708c3d0d3cc08f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f33d9d539fb94e5a17589c2dfe271ff9bb64904", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14995c4250f04b58bf6fc00e0e973a2e1b3cfb9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2419aa74081007dc4d14ff5640659052dfdfd69a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34f2a2f32af570dfcc532ad70c080629ee1c32b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1a61366933224b3ad80975c4d01ac2cc6931ecf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6c4250b81bd30beae94e1b7a4b26fa1193ad2e4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rwc8-9546-9gw5", "CVE-2026-68131"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "175efcfb-a5d5-342e-adad-df2ead862ad9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "1bc8fc7a-0a13-398f-92cc-ee904a1d8089", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "1e15253f-bcb7-3ed2-8f61-1f6af5778ca9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "2340aba0-a602-3ed6-b41f-51c7074b07c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <2419aa74081007dc4d14ff5640659052dfdfd69a"}, {"id": "342b1943-e477-3bae-bb06-22b8b7bd9343", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "5635ae27-7829-31bb-9a5c-974a16c456c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <14995c4250f04b58bf6fc00e0e973a2e1b3cfb9b"}, {"id": "7784e078-c650-3bb2-897f-240d9b9e354b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "811c4bf0-3ba7-373f-8519-fff8053fe594", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "accdc027-df29-3380-990b-68901c156614", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "b045c085-fba4-3fef-83e1-8fa43780bd81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <da926959bf791441ba06a80571708c3d0d3cc08f"}, {"id": "b9f480c6-f77e-35ea-aaeb-df736a5ca689", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <b1a61366933224b3ad80975c4d01ac2cc6931ecf"}, {"id": "bd97f249-35dd-3357-80bd-70fdef7abc94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <a6c4250b81bd30beae94e1b7a4b26fa1193ad2e4"}, {"id": "c7c9b88a-c35d-3643-86d5-6907a76febd1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d43c8c22-f75c-3e86-ac6e-74f5b8867282", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <6f33d9d539fb94e5a17589c2dfe271ff9bb64904"}, {"id": "d56838db-bde8-34e9-9b3c-fb00870096b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <34f2a2f32af570dfcc532ad70c080629ee1c32b0"}, {"id": "dc8c9776-9208-3454-b824-8286c8fe77f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "ddf49a16-533b-3ee2-b94e-a2602c298cfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "ff3f02d2-28e1-3101-8dd0-d587911126a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e8bd51bb0469d1a524130a057f894ff632376a <cf1167292f606deaddac35ec384eba48f08a68d2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b85ddf6d-fda1-3b0c-bd7b-0dcd9fd9c2af", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}